# Cloudflare Workers static-assets header rules. Not served; consumed at build time.
#
# The CSP is the point of this file. The privacy policy claims that opening a page
# here contacts nobody but this domain, and that there is no JavaScript on the site.
# These two lines make the browser enforce both, so the claim survives a careless
# edit rather than depending on one.
#
# `style-src 'self'` and no 'unsafe-inline': every rule lives in css/site.css.
# `img-src 'self' data:` — the marble veining in that stylesheet is an inline
# data: SVG, so dropping `data:` would strip the texture off every page.
# `media-src 'self'` — the home page's hero film. Under `default-src 'none'` a
# <video> is blocked outright with no visible error beyond an empty box, so this
# directive is load-bearing rather than decorative: remove it and the top of the
# front page silently goes blank. It stays `'self'`, which is the whole point —
# the film is served from this domain and there is no embed to phone anybody.
# When the playable demo lands it will need `script-src 'self'`; narrow that to
# the demo's own path rather than opening it up site-wide, and update the
# privacy policy in the same commit.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# The stylesheet is the only asset heavy enough to be worth caching hard, and it
# is the one most likely to change. Left on the default so a deploy is visible
# immediately; revisit with a hashed filename if it ever matters.

# /media/* is now the heaviest thing on the site by an order of magnitude — the
# film alone is 400KB against a 12KB page — and unlike the stylesheet it is
# finished art that changes when new art is drawn, not when a rule is tweaked.
# A day is deliberately modest rather than `immutable`: these filenames are not
# content-hashed, so anything longer means replacing a picture in place leaves
# readers looking at the old one with no way to say so.
/media/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
